  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important first step is to establish a clear performance floor. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest possible configuration: a linear-dimensionality-reduced RNA representation with no learned encoder, no aggregation, and no fusion. This gives a well-defined baseline that (1) tells me whether RNA signal alone is informative for the task, (2) provides a reference accuracy against which all more complex choices (learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, fusion) can be measured, and (3) is the fastest and least risky experiment to run, preserving budget for later exploration. In experiment 2 I can then swap in a learned RNA encoder (e.g., scvi_n200 or scgpt) while holding everything else constant, cleanly isolating the effect of representation quality."
}

